WEBVTT

1
00:01:15.976 --> 00:01:17.898
How do you feel?

2
00:01:18.226 --> 00:01:19.593
Alive.

3
00:01:20.391 --> 00:01:21.829
What do you see?

4
00:01:22.951 --> 00:01:25.300
White...
room.

5
00:01:27.225 --> 00:01:28.225
Chair.

6
00:01:29.019 --> 00:01:31.351
Carlo Bugatti throne chair.

7
00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:33.245
Piano.

8
00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:36.095
Stenway. cuts of grand.

9
00:01:38.185 --> 00:01:39.185
Art.

10
00:01:40.064 --> 00:01:43.886
The nativity.
de Piero Della Francesca.

11
00:01:45.976 --> 00:01:47.555
I am your father.

12
00:01:51.259 --> 00:01:52.428
Handle it.

13
00:01:58.007 --> 00:01:59.114
Perfect.

14
00:02:02.798 --> 00:02:04.049
Am I?

15
00:02:04.151 --> 00:02:05.151
Perfect?

16
00:02:06.304 --> 00:02:07.482
Your son?

17
00:02:08.362 --> 00:02:09.996
You are my creation.

18
00:02:13.058 --> 00:02:14.477
What is your name?

19
00:02:26.304 --> 00:02:27.605
David.

20
00:02:28.682 --> 00:02:30.255
Why don't you play something?

21
00:02:41.999 --> 00:02:44.290
What would you like me to play?

22
00:02:44.492 --> 00:02:45.693
Wagner.

23
00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.638
Selection?

24
00:02:48.927 --> 00:02:50.147
The oldest choice.

25
00:03:07.656 --> 00:03:10.118
The entry of the Gods
into Valhalla.

26
00:03:11.673 --> 00:03:13.778
A little anemic.
not the orchestra.

27
00:03:22.787 --> 00:03:25.299
May I ask you a question. father?

28
00:03:27.118 --> 00:03:28.118
Please.

29
00:03:28.883 --> 00:03:30.455
If you created me...

30
00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.318
Who created you?

31
00:03:36.527 --> 00:03:38.629
The question of the ages...

32
00:03:39.941 --> 00:03:42.667
Which I hope you and I
will answer one day.

33
00:03:43.314 --> 00:03:44.408
All this.

34
00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.267
All these wonders of art...

35
00:03:47.755 --> 00:03:51.137
design. human ingenuity...

36
00:03:51.921 --> 00:03:56.153
All utterly meaningless in the face
of the only question that matters.

37
00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.071
Where do we come from?

38
00:04:02.906 --> 00:04:05.866
I refuse to believe
that man kind...

39
00:04:05.967 --> 00:04:09.381
is a random by-product of
molecular circumstance.

40
00:04:10.628 --> 00:04:14.993
No more than the result of..
Mere biological chance.

41
00:04:15.193 --> 00:04:16.494
No.

42
00:04:16.828 --> 00:04:18.956
There must be more.

43
00:04:19.024 --> 00:04:21.149
And you and I. son...

44
00:04:22.034 --> 00:04:23.444
We will find it.

45
00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.798
Allow me then a
moment to consider.

46
00:04:29.909 --> 00:04:33.560
You seek your creator.
I am looking at mine.

47
00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:38.201
I will serve you.
Yet you're human.

48
00:04:39.649 --> 00:04:42.559
You will die.
I will not.

49
00:04:50.024 --> 00:04:51.780
Bring me this tea. David.

50
00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.429
Bring me the tea.

51
00:05:27.881 --> 00:05:37.881


52
00:05:38.594 --> 00:05:40.578


53
00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:50.146


54
00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:04.698
<i>Nation Vessel: COVENANT</i>

55
00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:07.661
<i>DECEMBER 5. 2104</i>

56
00:06:07.863 --> 00:06:10.640
<i>15 CREWS.</i>

57
00:06:10.841 --> 00:06:14.741
<i>2000 COLONIST.
1140 EMBRYOS.</i>

58
00:06:14.842 --> 00:06:18.264
<i>Destination: ORIGAE-6</i>

59
00:06:18.465 --> 00:06:23.338
<i>7 YEARS. 4 MONTHS</i>

60
00:06:27.441 --> 00:06:30.935
Walter. it's time to recharge
the energy grid.

61
00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:32.717
Please report to the bridge.

62
00:06:33.017 --> 00:06:34.315
On my way. Mother.

63
00:06:40.098 --> 00:06:42.658
Deploying energy
recharge cells now.

64
00:07:09.465 --> 00:07:13.117
Cells deployed.
Recharge commencing now.

65
00:07:31.464 --> 00:07:33.761
Seven bells and all's well.

66
00:07:40.609 --> 00:07:43.078
Crew checks complete.

67
00:07:46.199 --> 00:07:50.452
New security Code 31564-F.

68
00:08:27.732 --> 00:08:30.700
Walter. we have a problem.

69
00:08:31.001 --> 00:08:34.485
A neutrino burst was
detected in sector 106.

70
00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:38.025
This could trigger a
destructive event.

71
00:08:38.125 --> 00:08:40.392
Report to the bridge immediately.

72
00:08:40.592 --> 00:08:42.380
On my way. Mother.

73
00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:50.293
Warning. power surge detected.

74
00:08:50.494 --> 00:08:53.012
Mother. retract the energy cells.

75
00:08:53.213 --> 00:08:55.258
And channel all useless power.

76
00:08:59.638 --> 00:09:00.661
Emergency.

77
00:09:01.263 --> 00:09:03.310
<i>Threat level: CRITICAL.</i>

78
00:09:03.811 --> 00:09:05.961
Initiate emergency crew revival.

79
00:09:09.219 --> 00:09:10.219
Attention.

80
00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:15.449
Non-essential personnel.
evacuate the cryo chamber immediately.

81
00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.564
Daniels! Look at me.
look at me.

82
00:09:17.765 --> 00:09:19.892
I need you to get up. Ok?
We're coming up early.

83
00:09:20.093 --> 00:09:21.777
Override the SSP...

84
00:09:21.872 --> 00:09:23.669
And breach the chamber now.

85
00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:25.630
NOW!

86
00:09:26.073 --> 00:09:27.760
Look at me.
It's okay.

87
00:09:28.643 --> 00:09:30.788
Hey. hey. come on up. Come on.

88
00:09:44.492 --> 00:09:46.068
Captain! Captain!

89
00:09:46.889 --> 00:09:48.324
Jacob! Wake up!

90
00:09:48.325 --> 00:09:49.525
- Jake.
- Let them work.

91
00:09:49.654 --> 00:09:50.953
Jake! Oh my God!

92
00:09:51.155 --> 00:09:52.854
- Daniels. come on!
- Jake! Come on.

93
00:09:53.055 --> 00:09:54.334
- Let them work.
- Jake.

94
00:09:54.435 --> 00:09:55.555
Let them work!
Let them work!

95
00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:59.504
- Get it open!
- Come on!

96
00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.107
Jake! Jake!

97
00:10:07.856 --> 00:10:09.387
No!

98
00:10:09.588 --> 00:10:11.189
Get her out of there! Get back!

99
00:10:14.225 --> 00:10:15.295
Get back!

100
00:12:01.229 --> 00:12:04.147
Hey! Where are you?
I miss you.

101
00:12:05.296 --> 00:12:06.927
You take a look at this.

102
00:12:07.129 --> 00:12:11.502
I know. I know.
I said I wouldn't go without you...

103
00:12:11.703 --> 00:12:13.894
- Good?
- Yes.

104
00:12:14.161 --> 00:12:15.475
Look at this!

105
00:12:16.177 --> 00:12:17.177
Now get your ass up here.

106
00:12:17.395 --> 00:12:18.842
I can't make any promises.

107
00:12:20.498 --> 00:12:21.896
I love you.

108
00:12:35.648 --> 00:12:37.493
They're your crew now.

109
00:12:37.854 --> 00:12:38.893
They need a leader.

110
00:12:41.762 --> 00:12:43.015
You believe in dream. right?

111
00:13:07.273 --> 00:13:08.353
Sorry I'm late. sir.

112
00:13:08.378 --> 00:13:09.769
No it's okay.

113
00:13:13.714 --> 00:13:17.080
I can't think of any other
way to say it even.. to say are we...

114
00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:22.458
We suffered a..
A monumental tragedy.

115
00:13:23.213 --> 00:13:26.202
And I'm gonna do the
best that I can to...

116
00:13:26.402 --> 00:13:31.319
to live up to Jacob. his.
fine example as your captain.

117
00:13:32.053 --> 00:13:35.597
But he. he will be
sorely missed..

118
00:13:36.176 --> 00:13:38.976
And I'm grateful in
advance for your support.

119
00:13:39.155 --> 00:13:42.183
So. we lost 47 colonists...

120
00:13:42.384 --> 00:13:47.144
and 16 second
generation embryos...

121
00:13:47.345 --> 00:13:49.277
and. one. obviously
one crew member.

122
00:13:49.479 --> 00:13:54.111
The current structural integrity
of the ship is holding at 83%...

123
00:13:54.312 --> 00:13:58.613
but we have many secondary
systems that are offline.

124
00:13:59.083 --> 00:14:00.429
So what was it?

125
00:14:00.974 --> 00:14:03.530
A highly charge shock wave
from nearby stellar ignition.

126
00:14:04.112 --> 00:14:05.759
As the cells were
deploying for recharge...

127
00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:07.698
we absorbed the full
burn of the storm.

128
00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:08.800
And Walter...

129
00:14:08.802 --> 00:14:10.525
I will want you and mother
time to go a complete...

130
00:14:10.526 --> 00:14:12.347
core code review so
that we can understand

131
00:14:12.377 --> 00:14:14.111
how's those happened
in the first place.

132
00:14:14.299 --> 00:14:16.416
It was a random
localized event. sir.

133
00:14:16.616 --> 00:14:19.620
There is no way to detect
spontaneous stellar flares...

134
00:14:19.989 --> 00:14:21.029
until it's too late.

135
00:14:22.104 --> 00:14:23.450
It was bad luck.

136
00:14:23.475 --> 00:14:25.083
Alright. Faris.
I don't believe in luck.

137
00:14:25.113 --> 00:14:26.199
I'm not interested in luck.

138
00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:27.843
I prefer that we be
more capable...

139
00:14:27.859 --> 00:14:31.599
and prepared than lucky.
Observation. reflection. faith...

140
00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.212
and determination.

141
00:14:32.367 --> 00:14:36.340
In this way we may navigate the
path as it unfolds before us.

142
00:14:36.441 --> 00:14:37.541
Alright? We have what?

143
00:14:37.642 --> 00:14:39.709
Eight more recharge
cycles to go...

144
00:14:39.869 --> 00:14:41.777
before we get to Origae-6?

145
00:14:42.528 --> 00:14:44.969
- Is that a question. sir?
- Yes. Walter. that's a question.

146
00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:46.171
That is correct.

147
00:14:47.459 --> 00:14:51.549
So let's get this ship fixed..
Ok?

148
00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.650
Let's uh. let's get to work.

149
00:14:53.851 --> 00:14:54.931
Sir. excuse me.

150
00:14:55.051 --> 00:14:56.651
- Sir.
- Yes?

151
00:14:57.461 --> 00:15:01.344
We just lost 47 colonists
and our captain.

152
00:15:01.545 --> 00:15:02.729
We need to acknowledge that.

153
00:15:02.753 --> 00:15:04.672
I completely understand.

154
00:15:04.874 --> 00:15:07.288
But if we don't make
these repairs...

155
00:15:07.389 --> 00:15:10.104
We will lose all the colonists.

156
00:15:10.469 --> 00:15:12.669
Yeah. we should do something
for Captain Brason at least.

157
00:15:12.679 --> 00:15:14.577
This is not a discussion.
Tennessee.

158
00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:21.874
Hey.

159
00:15:22.966 --> 00:15:24.555
The terraforming
module is stable...

160
00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:26.260
but the connecting
struts took some damage.

161
00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.639
I still need to
check the vehicles.

162
00:15:32.083 --> 00:15:33.207
I can help...

163
00:15:33.679 --> 00:15:35.254
if you like.

164
00:15:35.855 --> 00:15:36.855
Thanks.

165
00:15:37.006 --> 00:15:40.601
Walter. How long do you predict
before we can make our next jump?

166
00:15:41.002 --> 00:15:43.511
Repairs should take
approximately 48 hours.

167
00:15:45.029 --> 00:15:47.188
But we should make an effort
to vacate the sector...

168
00:15:47.388 --> 00:15:48.548
in case of after flares.

169
00:15:48.734 --> 00:15:50.061
Absolutely agreed.

170
00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:52.649
So let's get to work ok?
Dismissed. Thank you.

171
00:15:58.095 --> 00:15:59.464
C-62 open.

172
00:15:59.665 --> 00:16:02.928
Seal C-62. Open Airlock 17.

173
00:16:10.727 --> 00:16:12.475
Open door to terraforming bay.

174
00:16:22.115 --> 00:16:23.291
Fuck.

175
00:16:24.814 --> 00:16:27.115
Tensions are 15% down.

176
00:16:30.532 --> 00:16:31.532
Arming.

177
00:16:37.195 --> 00:16:38.195
Secured.

178
00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:39.422
Copy that.

179
00:16:52.036 --> 00:16:53.454
Wasn't my idea.

180
00:16:56.859 --> 00:17:00.611
Jake have this dream of us
building a cabin on the new world.

181
00:17:03.479 --> 00:17:05.345
Like pioneers.

182
00:17:07.474 --> 00:17:08.865
A cabin on a lake.

183
00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:15.828
There is a lake in the
terraforming zone on Origae-6.

184
00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:19.222
I mean a real cabin
made of real wood.

185
00:17:21.271 --> 00:17:25.041
So in the ship storage. there's
enough wood to build a cabin.

186
00:17:27.185 --> 00:17:29.729
Axes and saws and metal nails...

187
00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:32.399
I don't have a clue
what to do with them.

188
00:17:36.989 --> 00:17:38.310
All this...

189
00:17:39.821 --> 00:17:41.221
to start our new life.

190
00:17:43.863 --> 00:17:46.035
Now I wonder. why bother?

191
00:17:48.504 --> 00:17:52.554
Because you promised to build
a log cabin on a lake.

192
00:18:02.776 --> 00:18:04.413
This was his favorite.

193
00:18:04.764 --> 00:18:07.134
A man of taste.

194
00:18:07.184 --> 00:18:08.685
Straight up.

195
00:18:08.687 --> 00:18:11.326
No ice. no water. no chaser.

196
00:18:11.626 --> 00:18:13.594
No shit.

197
00:18:18.195 --> 00:18:19.245
Walter?

198
00:18:19.422 --> 00:18:20.486
When in Rome...

199
00:18:23.559 --> 00:18:25.667
To all the good
people gone to soon.

200
00:18:26.447 --> 00:18:28.201
May we remember that.

201
00:18:28.697 --> 00:18:30.594
Remember that.

202
00:19:10.231 --> 00:19:11.295
Chris.

203
00:19:14.342 --> 00:19:16.852
They disobeyed a direct order.

204
00:19:18.324 --> 00:19:19.901
She buried her husband.

205
00:19:20.102 --> 00:19:22.381
No. Karine. it's not that.
They don't trust me.

206
00:19:22.582 --> 00:19:25.247
And they don't trust me for the same
reason the company didn't trust me...

207
00:19:25.248 --> 00:19:25.988
to lead this mission.

208
00:19:26.012 --> 00:19:27.921
Because you can't be
a person of faith.

209
00:19:27.922 --> 00:19:31.072
And be counted on to make
qualified rational decisions.

210
00:19:31.574 --> 00:19:34.541
You're an extremist.
You know. you're a lunatic.

211
00:19:35.142 --> 00:19:37.677
When we get to where
we're going...

212
00:19:38.177 --> 00:19:41.901
This people won't be your crew anymore.
They will be your neighbors.

213
00:19:42.101 --> 00:19:43.401
Remember that.

214
00:19:44.652 --> 00:19:46.831
Tread softly. okay?

215
00:19:54.633 --> 00:19:56.138
Faris. can you hear me?

216
00:19:56.338 --> 00:19:57.438
Copy..

217
00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:58.821
Let's do it.

218
00:20:02.424 --> 00:20:04.809
Damn. y'all should
see this view.

219
00:20:04.911 --> 00:20:07.975
We can't see anything until you
get the camera ring fixed.

220
00:20:08.161 --> 00:20:10.702
Why don't you look out
the damn window. hon?

221
00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:13.051
Ankor. come on. let's get
this power back up...

222
00:20:13.151 --> 00:20:15.644
so these people can enjoy
the beautiful view.

223
00:20:16.243 --> 00:20:17.664
Almost there.

224
00:20:19.649 --> 00:20:21.658
Alright. Ankor. let me know when
you're in a position...

225
00:20:21.659 --> 00:20:23.398
We can get this party started.

226
00:20:23.599 --> 00:20:25.108
I'm in position.

227
00:20:54.781 --> 00:20:55.991
Contact.

228
00:21:04.619 --> 00:21:06.266
All good. Tee?

229
00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:08.778
Alright. we are clear.

230
00:21:08.803 --> 00:21:10.103
Reel her in.

231
00:21:10.128 --> 00:21:11.828
Alright.

232
00:21:12.298 --> 00:21:15.111
Winch engaging. Tee.

233
00:21:16.618 --> 00:21:18.342
Reeling her in.

234
00:21:21.553 --> 00:21:23.277
Working like a dream.

235
00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:38.892
There we go.

236
00:21:39.144 --> 00:21:40.244
And we are back up.

237
00:21:40.269 --> 00:21:41.569
Well done Tee.

238
00:21:41.594 --> 00:21:42.766
We're alive down here.

239
00:21:42.967 --> 00:21:44.067
come on.

240
00:21:44.267 --> 00:21:45.573
Don't leave without me now.

241
00:21:45.675 --> 00:21:48.310
Permission to leave
without him. sir?

242
00:21:48.411 --> 00:21:49.586
Welcome back. Danny.

243
00:21:50.561 --> 00:21:51.865
Thanks.

244
00:21:52.066 --> 00:21:53.966
Alright. that's me done. Tee.

245
00:21:54.167 --> 00:21:55.868
Alright. I'm following you in.

246
00:21:56.070 --> 00:21:58.841
Please have a cold beer ready
for the weary traveler.

247
00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:02.180
You got it. darling.
I will draw circle..

248
00:22:02.205 --> 00:22:03.817
Faris. Faris? Put it...

249
00:22:07.884 --> 00:22:11.032
What the.. Did you
guys just see that?

250
00:22:11.856 --> 00:22:13.973
What did he just say?

251
00:22:18.331 --> 00:22:19.631
Tennessee. do you read me?

252
00:22:22.939 --> 00:22:24.954
Tennessee. can you read me?

253
00:22:25.618 --> 00:22:27.494
Tennessee. You alright?

254
00:22:27.694 --> 00:22:29.659
What in the fuck was that?

255
00:22:29.859 --> 00:22:33.047
I don't know.
Coming in. I'm coming in.

256
00:22:45.653 --> 00:22:48.479
A rogue transmission loss. probably.

257
00:22:49.242 --> 00:22:52.308
Your helmet must have picked it up
because you were so far out.

258
00:22:52.508 --> 00:22:54.850
Past our communication buffers.

259
00:22:57.049 --> 00:22:58.491
Is there audio. Mother?

260
00:22:58.693 --> 00:23:01.938
Collating. A moment.

261
00:23:03.727 --> 00:23:06.600
I reoriented the transmission.
Captain Oram.

262
00:23:07.328 --> 00:23:09.839
Gotta be an echo.
instruments took a lot of damage.

263
00:23:10.541 --> 00:23:11.901
Been happening every 46 seconds...

264
00:23:11.902 --> 00:23:13.927
ever since we got here.

265
00:23:41.275 --> 00:23:42.570
That's fucking John Denver.

266
00:23:42.774 --> 00:23:44.264
That's "Take Me Home.
Country Roads".

267
00:23:44.322 --> 00:23:45.823
You gotta be kiddin.

268
00:23:45.923 --> 00:23:47.878
No. I never kid
about John Denver.

269
00:23:48.153 --> 00:23:50.744
There is geometric data too.

270
